<title>USA: Paccar Q3 sales down, shr falls to $1.31.</title>
<headline>Paccar Q3 sales down, shr falls to $1.31.</headline>
<dateline>BELLEVUE, Wash. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in millions of dollars(a))</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended  Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>					Sept. 30	    Sept. 30</p>
<p>				    1996	1995     1996     1995</p>
<p>Manufacturing and Parts</p>
<p>  Net Sales		  $1,046.8 $1,147.0 $3,108.4  $3,476.0</p>
<p>Financial Services</p>
<p>  Revenues			 66.8     65.1    200.3     188.2</p>
<p>Income Before Taxes:</p>
<p>   Manufacturing and Parts   55.6     73.7    146.8     221.1</p>
<p>   Financial Services	  16.9     14.6     50.3	39.6</p>
<p>   Investment Income	    7.8	7.1     20.9	20.1</p>
<p>   Other			     .5     13.6	1.2	14.9</p>
<p>Total Income Before</p>
<p>  Income Taxes		   80.8    109.0    219.2     295.7</p>
<p>   Income Taxes		  29.7     40.7     80.7     108.0</p>
<p> Net Income			51.1     68.3  138.5(b)    187.7</p>
<p> Net Income Per Share	  1.31     1.76     3.56	4.83</p>
<p>(a)  Except per share amounts.</p>
<p>(b)  Includes $11 million of after-tax costs to eliminate excess truck production capacity.</p>
<p>NOTE: Third quarter net of $51.1 million includes a $7.5 million gain from favorable resolution of litigation involving environmental cost reimbursements.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610.</p>
